1
00:00:00,163 --> 00:00:01,561
(This drama complied with production
guidelines for filming child actors,)

2
00:00:01,563 --> 00:00:03,000
(and some scenes used
generative AI technology.)

3
00:00:03,652 --> 00:00:06,126
(Episode 42)

4
00:00:08,491 --> 00:00:10,340
Welcome. What are you looking for?

5
00:00:11,177 --> 00:00:12,250
Well...

6
00:00:28,404 --> 00:00:29,574
Clothes for your wife?

7
00:00:30,045 --> 00:00:31,258
Yes.

8
00:00:31,283 --> 00:00:32,896
What kind of clothes does she like?

9
00:00:35,568 --> 00:00:36,988
How about this dress?

10
00:00:37,645 --> 00:00:39,538
Yes. I think she'll like it.

11
00:00:39,562 --> 00:00:41,183
What size?

12
00:00:41,352 --> 00:00:43,680
About the same size.

13
00:00:45,598 --> 00:00:47,885
You really...

14
00:00:47,909 --> 00:00:51,871
have quite an eye for women.

15
00:00:51,895 --> 00:00:53,410
Seriously.

16
00:00:55,018 --> 00:00:57,594
You're not offended, are you?
I was just joking.

17
00:00:57,595 --> 00:00:59,341
Not at all.

18
00:01:00,778 --> 00:01:03,617
You're such a caring husband.

19
00:01:04,654 --> 00:01:06,887
Come back if she likes it.

20
00:01:07,876 --> 00:01:09,749
Sure. I will.

21
00:01:10,316 --> 00:01:13,306
- Here you go. Thank you.
- Thank you.

22
00:01:31,165 --> 00:01:34,643
Must be nice.
Having a husband buy you clothes.

23
00:01:37,891 --> 00:01:41,336
Maybe I should've treated him better
when he was alive.

24
00:01:50,391 --> 00:01:51,391
Yes.

25
00:01:56,425 --> 00:01:57,621
I'm Do Do Hee.

26
00:01:58,073 --> 00:01:59,481
I know.

27
00:02:00,938 --> 00:02:03,190
You're exactly the character
we were looking for.

28
00:02:03,529 --> 00:02:04,733
Really?

29
00:02:08,418 --> 00:02:09,979
You work at a publishing company?

30
00:02:10,003 --> 00:02:11,003
Yes.

31
00:02:11,412 --> 00:02:13,358
I'm very interested
in children's fairy tale books.

32
00:02:13,382 --> 00:02:14,628
You're not what I expected.

33
00:02:14,652 --> 00:02:15,862
I get that a lot.

34
00:02:24,972 --> 00:02:26,090
Thank you.

35
00:02:28,564 --> 00:02:29,958
You have a lot of followers.

36
00:02:30,577 --> 00:02:32,371
They've been dropping lately,
so I'm upset.

37
00:02:32,395 --> 00:02:33,679
Let's get them back up.

38
00:02:33,831 --> 00:02:35,643
What, are you aiming for a million?

39
00:02:35,852 --> 00:02:37,406
Why not?

40
00:02:38,350 --> 00:02:40,037
I like your confidence.

41
00:02:41,118 --> 00:02:43,730
But I'm not sure
if I should appear on a show like this.

42
00:02:43,867 --> 00:02:44,920
My father is...

43
00:02:44,945 --> 00:02:47,981
We can keep your family ties confidential.
That's standard.

44
00:02:48,471 --> 00:02:49,603
That's reassuring.

45
00:02:50,465 --> 00:02:53,442
But I'm worried
because my fiancé is a bit sensitive.

46
00:02:56,519 --> 00:02:58,383
When are you getting married?

47
00:02:59,059 --> 00:03:00,901
You can get married after the show ends.

48
00:03:01,452 --> 00:03:03,595
Why wouldn't he want a famous wife?

49
00:03:03,626 --> 00:03:06,335
Ordinary people probably think
it's that simple.

50
00:03:06,372 --> 00:03:07,912
You'd better think carefully
before deciding.

51
00:03:08,532 --> 00:03:11,527
We reached out to you first,

52
00:03:11,782 --> 00:03:14,915
so to put it simply,
you're the star of this show.

53
00:03:15,151 --> 00:03:16,525
You can't change your mind.

54
00:03:16,549 --> 00:03:17,635
"The star?"

55
00:03:18,185 --> 00:03:19,988
- Me?
- Of course.

56
00:03:20,015 --> 00:03:22,404
Do you know how much searching I did
to find you?

57
00:03:22,766 --> 00:03:24,104
You went that far...

58
00:03:24,912 --> 00:03:26,462
Let me think about it first.

59
00:03:28,264 --> 00:03:29,264
Excuse me.

60
00:03:38,485 --> 00:03:39,712
What on earth is this?

61
00:03:44,285 --> 00:03:45,571
Seriously.

62
00:03:47,102 --> 00:03:49,545
Wait here. I'll get you one.

63
00:03:53,731 --> 00:03:56,569
He's just naturally suited
to being an assistant director.

64
00:03:56,974 --> 00:03:58,489
Please wait a moment.

65
00:04:03,792 --> 00:04:07,417
If you take a close look
at our program proposal,

66
00:04:07,577 --> 00:04:09,907
I think
you'll be able to convince your fiancé.

67
00:04:10,109 --> 00:04:11,228
You think so?

68
00:04:14,172 --> 00:04:15,525
Do Do Hee is a good choice, right?

69
00:04:16,069 --> 00:04:17,615
She's definitely our female bombshell.

70
00:04:17,776 --> 00:04:18,815
She's a real femme fatale.

71
00:04:19,505 --> 00:04:21,387
She'll definitely appeal to the guys.

72
00:04:22,064 --> 00:04:23,124
Exactly.

73
00:04:23,432 --> 00:04:25,695
It's reassuring to have you approve.

74
00:04:29,078 --> 00:04:30,788
You acted like you weren't coming,

75
00:04:30,812 --> 00:04:32,374
but what do you think? Pretty nice, right?

76
00:04:32,838 --> 00:04:35,092
You must be the CEO.

77
00:04:35,305 --> 00:04:36,480
Hello.

78
00:04:36,505 --> 00:04:38,095
I love the office.

79
00:04:38,119 --> 00:04:40,204
- Thank you.
- Hello.

80
00:04:41,285 --> 00:04:43,252
- Why are you here?
- It's my routine.

81
00:04:43,703 --> 00:04:46,095
I even put away my cello
so it wouldn't get in your way.

82
00:04:48,072 --> 00:04:51,703
The CEO is absolutely gorgeous.
And she's tall too.

83
00:04:52,272 --> 00:04:54,901
Remember I told you about senior modeling?

84
00:04:55,205 --> 00:04:56,391
She's perfect for it.

85
00:04:56,866 --> 00:04:58,340
"A senior model?"

86
00:04:59,181 --> 00:05:02,110
I've been getting called
a model a lot lately.

87
00:05:03,504 --> 00:05:05,318
Just focus on one thing.

88
00:05:05,885 --> 00:05:07,040
Fine.

89
00:05:07,065 --> 00:05:09,086
So your thing is giving
people a hard time.

90
00:05:09,111 --> 00:05:10,538
It's really hard for me.

91
00:05:10,664 --> 00:05:12,118
This is the junior I ended up with.

92
00:05:12,143 --> 00:05:14,807
As long as he does his job well,
that's enough. Take care.

93
00:05:17,384 --> 00:05:19,263
She's totally my type.

94
00:05:19,933 --> 00:05:21,508
She's got star quality too.

95
00:05:22,295 --> 00:05:25,346
Hey, how come you're not doing anything
with someone like that around you?

96
00:05:26,417 --> 00:05:28,933
Stop trying to use everyone around you.

97
00:05:28,958 --> 00:05:31,216
I don't like it,
and she likes it even less.

98
00:05:32,892 --> 00:05:35,426
Let's just show them up to this point
for episode one.

99
00:05:35,451 --> 00:05:36,451
However,

100
00:05:36,759 --> 00:05:38,735
decide whether we start with an interview,

101
00:05:38,737 --> 00:05:40,909
or a conversation.

102
00:05:42,334 --> 00:05:44,468
You decide. I'm just good
at setting things up.

103
00:05:44,652 --> 00:05:45,750
That's all I know.

104
00:05:59,571 --> 00:06:00,961
Excuse me...

105
00:06:03,087 --> 00:06:04,087
What?

106
00:06:06,052 --> 00:06:09,477
I was hoping to get some pictures
of your mom.

107
00:06:10,632 --> 00:06:11,769
"Pictures of my mom?"

108
00:06:19,512 --> 00:06:22,193
Why are you doing all this
for him to propose to her?

109
00:06:22,504 --> 00:06:24,822
I said I'd help them.

110
00:06:25,132 --> 00:06:27,681
I want her to be happy.

111
00:06:27,972 --> 00:06:30,751
You people might be against it,

112
00:06:30,775 --> 00:06:32,005
and you might not like me,

113
00:06:32,029 --> 00:06:33,918
- getting involved...
- Enough.

114
00:06:34,176 --> 00:06:35,754
Stop talking. Hey,

115
00:06:35,779 --> 00:06:37,618
what's with "you people"?

116
00:06:38,832 --> 00:06:40,940
Then what should I call you?

117
00:06:43,645 --> 00:06:46,138
What kind of pictures do you need?

118
00:06:46,307 --> 00:06:48,607
About that...

119
00:06:49,478 --> 00:06:51,678
From when she was young,

120
00:06:51,694 --> 00:06:54,777
when she was a little older,
before and after she got married,

121
00:06:55,168 --> 00:06:58,127
- and after she had you two.
- Got it.

122
00:06:58,152 --> 00:07:00,854
I'll pick some out and give them
to you later. Ten should be enough, right?

123
00:07:01,636 --> 00:07:03,154
Yeah. That's plenty.

124
00:07:04,317 --> 00:07:05,550
Thank you.

125
00:07:06,938 --> 00:07:07,938
And...

126
00:07:08,792 --> 00:07:10,780
I heard you joined a new show.

127
00:07:10,804 --> 00:07:12,399
- Congratulations.
- Thanks.

128
00:07:12,424 --> 00:07:13,709
I met your friend too.

129
00:07:13,733 --> 00:07:15,443
I heard.

130
00:07:15,467 --> 00:07:16,467
I'll go then.

131
00:07:17,418 --> 00:07:19,015
Come visit the set sometime.

132
00:07:19,785 --> 00:07:22,260
You're friends, aren't you?
Aren't you going to root for her?

133
00:07:23,745 --> 00:07:24,931
Can I come?

134
00:07:26,285 --> 00:07:27,285
I'll come.

135
00:07:41,452 --> 00:07:43,740
Jung A, he told me to come visit the set.

136
00:07:43,765 --> 00:07:45,145
When do you start filming?

137
00:07:45,840 --> 00:07:48,153
I was so surprised
when he suddenly told me.

138
00:07:48,357 --> 00:07:50,007
- Who?
- Who do you think?

139
00:07:50,032 --> 00:07:51,360
That guy at our house...

140
00:07:52,395 --> 00:07:54,611
The director? Your second brother?

141
00:07:54,636 --> 00:07:56,792
I told you not to call him that.

142
00:07:57,572 --> 00:07:59,027
But what should I bring?

143
00:07:59,052 --> 00:08:00,850
Should I buy a gift?

144
00:08:01,547 --> 00:08:02,744
You like it that much?

145
00:08:03,796 --> 00:08:04,796
Yeah.

146
00:08:05,339 --> 00:08:07,550
It'll be my first time on a set like that,

147
00:08:07,574 --> 00:08:08,748
so I think it'll be exciting.

148
00:08:10,140 --> 00:08:11,227
Okay.

149
00:08:11,646 --> 00:08:12,646
Yeah.

150
00:08:22,732 --> 00:08:23,826
What?

151
00:08:28,265 --> 00:08:29,707
Any news about Mai?

152
00:08:31,411 --> 00:08:32,596
Didn't she go to Vietnam?

153
00:08:33,205 --> 00:08:34,991
I called my father-in-law,

154
00:08:36,121 --> 00:08:37,750
and he asked if Mai was doing okay.

155
00:08:38,532 --> 00:08:39,803
It seemed like he didn't know,

156
00:08:40,454 --> 00:08:42,047
so I just exchanged a few pleasantries
and hung up.

157
00:08:43,325 --> 00:08:44,797
If she's not in Vietnam,

158
00:08:45,019 --> 00:08:46,635
where on earth did she go?

159
00:08:47,232 --> 00:08:48,540
She can't be feeling well, either.

160
00:08:48,813 --> 00:08:50,623
I'm freezing. Turn off the fan.

161
00:08:50,837 --> 00:08:53,422
- Aren't you hot?
- I'm cold. Get out.

162
00:08:53,446 --> 00:08:54,529
You're cold?

163
00:08:54,900 --> 00:08:56,633
Seung Hyun, are you sick?

164
00:08:57,221 --> 00:08:58,479
I said get out.

165
00:08:59,214 --> 00:09:00,615
You are sick.

166
00:09:01,081 --> 00:09:02,396
I'll get you some herbal tonic.

167
00:09:02,593 --> 00:09:04,256
I don't even want
to look at the herbal tonic.

168
00:09:04,378 --> 00:09:06,761
- Just get me some medicine.
- What's wrong with the herbal tonic?

169
00:09:07,932 --> 00:09:09,245
Because that man gave it to...

170
00:09:09,269 --> 00:09:10,343
Seung Hyun!

171
00:09:12,802 --> 00:09:14,972
Okay. I'll go get some medicine.

172
00:09:35,851 --> 00:09:37,268
I heard you were sick.

173
00:09:37,577 --> 00:09:38,832
Take the day off.

174
00:09:41,171 --> 00:09:43,400
Are you really not going to talk to me?
What's wrong with you?

175
00:09:43,425 --> 00:09:44,709
How can I take a day off work?

176
00:09:45,148 --> 00:09:46,650
Stop making it sound so easy.

177
00:09:47,772 --> 00:09:50,614
O Reum got sick and left,
Mai left, and before that,

178
00:09:52,091 --> 00:09:53,671
that bastard
who calls himself my father...

179
00:09:54,331 --> 00:09:56,136
I couldn't even go to work
having to deal with everything for him.

180
00:09:56,432 --> 00:09:58,852
- How am I supposed to take a day off?
- Is all of that my fault?

181
00:09:59,942 --> 00:10:01,808
- Forget it.
- That's enough!

182
00:10:01,978 --> 00:10:03,497
You're really acting strange.

183
00:10:03,792 --> 00:10:06,147
Why do you keep
making me out to be the bad guy?

184
00:10:06,172 --> 00:10:08,373
When did I ever force Mai to leave?

185
00:10:08,611 --> 00:10:11,058
Or treat her badly enough
that she couldn't stand it?

186
00:10:11,083 --> 00:10:12,148
Mom!

187
00:10:12,758 --> 00:10:14,906
Mom, what are you doing?

188
00:10:15,242 --> 00:10:17,831
Seung Hyun is sick.
You need to understand.

189
00:10:18,070 --> 00:10:20,402
I understand.
That's why I'm acting like this.

190
00:10:20,427 --> 00:10:21,810
Do you think I don't have feelings?

191
00:10:23,088 --> 00:10:24,347
You think you're the only family she has?

192
00:10:24,486 --> 00:10:26,490
Mai is family to me too!

193
00:10:28,779 --> 00:10:31,072
That brat. Hey, Cha Seung Hyun!

194
00:10:31,533 --> 00:10:33,577
Mom, later.

195
00:10:33,601 --> 00:10:35,387
Okay? Later.

196
00:10:35,826 --> 00:10:37,892
Just let it go for today.

197
00:10:38,553 --> 00:10:40,019
Seriously.

198
00:10:51,278 --> 00:10:53,859
Yeong Ju, it's another hot morning.

199
00:10:54,338 --> 00:10:56,677
How about we watch a movie somewhere cool?

200
00:10:57,245 --> 00:10:59,769
I've already booked the tickets,
so I'll see you tonight.

201
00:11:02,398 --> 00:11:03,908
A movie? Now?

202
00:11:09,698 --> 00:11:10,786
What do I care?

203
00:11:11,558 --> 00:11:12,667
Those Cha bastards...

204
00:11:13,324 --> 00:11:14,324
What jerks.

205
00:11:17,892 --> 00:11:18,892
Sure.

206
00:11:19,139 --> 00:11:20,914
Pick something nice and cool.

207
00:11:45,602 --> 00:11:46,635
Yeong Ju.

208
00:11:47,549 --> 00:11:48,549
Yeong Ju?

209
00:11:49,890 --> 00:11:50,954
Yeong Ju.

210
00:11:53,178 --> 00:11:55,197
Let's put the photos in this order.

211
00:11:55,332 --> 00:11:57,897
Then the drawings will start here,
and the music will change too.

212
00:11:58,422 --> 00:11:59,444
What do you think?

213
00:11:59,547 --> 00:12:00,674
I like it.

214
00:12:02,519 --> 00:12:04,902
Let's use this font.

215
00:12:05,244 --> 00:12:07,632
And I'll add some drawings here.

216
00:12:07,656 --> 00:12:08,957
Looks good.

217
00:12:09,372 --> 00:12:11,388
Let's have them pop up one by one
when the slides change.

218
00:12:14,485 --> 00:12:15,685
That'll be cute.

219
00:12:22,070 --> 00:12:24,345
Let's eat something
before the bride and groom get here.

220
00:12:24,370 --> 00:12:25,574
Sounds good.

221
00:12:25,859 --> 00:12:27,590
I haven't really eaten today either.

222
00:12:27,749 --> 00:12:29,422
- What should we get?
- Let me think...

223
00:12:29,791 --> 00:12:31,008
- Hangover soup?
- Hangover soup?

224
00:12:31,411 --> 00:12:33,166
Do you like hangover soup?

225
00:12:34,305 --> 00:12:35,305
A little.

226
00:12:46,645 --> 00:12:47,730
I have a question.

227
00:12:48,625 --> 00:12:49,678
Don't get mad.

228
00:12:49,915 --> 00:12:51,235
Is it something I should get mad about?

229
00:12:51,259 --> 00:12:52,478
I don't know.

230
00:12:52,692 --> 00:12:54,581
You tend to get mad out of nowhere.

231
00:12:54,605 --> 00:12:55,605
Me?

232
00:13:00,478 --> 00:13:02,000
What's your question?

233
00:13:03,734 --> 00:13:05,987
The woman who's getting proposed to
is the grandma...

234
00:13:06,012 --> 00:13:07,356
of the child you donated
your bone marrow to.

235
00:13:08,705 --> 00:13:10,402
And to you, she's...

236
00:13:10,510 --> 00:13:12,056
I know what you're getting at.

237
00:13:12,612 --> 00:13:14,902
I used to dislike her too.

238
00:13:15,202 --> 00:13:18,214
It was more resentment than dislike.

239
00:13:19,392 --> 00:13:20,801
I'm not sure why,

240
00:13:22,378 --> 00:13:25,737
but she apologized to me the other day.

241
00:13:27,019 --> 00:13:28,890
She had nothing to apologize to me for.

242
00:13:29,858 --> 00:13:31,672
I felt so strange.

243
00:13:32,338 --> 00:13:34,861
I wasn't happy or sad...

244
00:13:34,949 --> 00:13:36,340
You don't have to say anything more.

245
00:13:37,258 --> 00:13:40,012
I don't know exactly how you feel,
but I can kind of guess.

246
00:13:40,036 --> 00:13:41,122
How?

247
00:13:41,882 --> 00:13:43,033
The Little Mermaid?

248
00:13:45,998 --> 00:13:48,666
- Let's eat and get going.
- Your face is turning red.

249
00:13:49,143 --> 00:13:50,609
Seriously!

250
00:13:51,444 --> 00:13:52,746
Eat.

251
00:13:54,245 --> 00:13:55,601
Your face is the same color as the soup.

252
00:13:56,517 --> 00:13:58,880
Popcorn is a must at the movies.

253
00:14:02,061 --> 00:14:03,414
- Have a seat.
- Okay.

254
00:14:09,218 --> 00:14:10,218
Well,

255
00:14:10,547 --> 00:14:12,789
how about a nice, refreshing movie?

256
00:14:42,659 --> 00:14:44,480
(Yeong Ju!)

257
00:14:44,488 --> 00:14:46,984
(Enough with the grandma act,)

258
00:14:46,999 --> 00:14:49,263
(and come into my arms now.)

259
00:14:53,602 --> 00:14:59,681
(Yeong Ju! You've done so well
as both a mom and a grandma.)

260
00:15:43,781 --> 00:15:48,447
(Let's spend the rest of our lives
together, just the two of us.)

261
00:15:48,470 --> 00:15:50,711
(As husband and wife.)

262
00:16:19,739 --> 00:16:21,681
(From here on,
the adult me will take over!)

263
00:16:44,805 --> 00:16:48,571
I'll finish what that child couldn't do.

264
00:17:02,599 --> 00:17:03,599
Yeong Ju,

265
00:17:06,372 --> 00:17:07,673
will you marry me?

266
00:17:12,478 --> 00:17:15,515
Pearls symbolize tears,
so I wasn't going to get one,

267
00:17:16,849 --> 00:17:18,210
but they say they can also mean,

268
00:17:18,691 --> 00:17:19,955
"no more tears."

269
00:17:23,605 --> 00:17:24,825
And most importantly,

270
00:17:27,438 --> 00:17:29,899
it's the ring that suits you best.

271
00:17:54,382 --> 00:17:55,869
Take your time answering.

272
00:17:56,772 --> 00:17:58,458
You don't have to decide today.

273
00:18:02,136 --> 00:18:05,196
Why would you go this far for me?
I'm no one special.

274
00:18:06,078 --> 00:18:07,421
Because I've finally found...

275
00:18:07,955 --> 00:18:09,207
my other half in you.

276
00:18:15,705 --> 00:18:17,360
My mom passed away when I was young,

277
00:18:18,594 --> 00:18:21,258
and I only lived with my brother,
so I never really knew what family was.

278
00:18:21,925 --> 00:18:22,985
But now...

279
00:18:24,193 --> 00:18:26,866
I want to build a beautiful family
with you.

280
00:18:28,859 --> 00:18:30,502
And of course, Seung Hyun, Seung Woo,

281
00:18:31,802 --> 00:18:32,818
all of us together.

282
00:19:37,678 --> 00:19:40,018
Is this pork trotters or porridge?

283
00:19:41,492 --> 00:19:43,292
Where did she go?

284
00:19:44,703 --> 00:19:45,703
Right.

285
00:19:49,518 --> 00:19:51,280
You were home?

286
00:19:54,252 --> 00:19:55,447
Are you still feeling sick?

287
00:20:00,598 --> 00:20:02,827
Let me see. Why are you so hot?

288
00:20:03,550 --> 00:20:04,617
Leave me alone.

289
00:20:05,892 --> 00:20:08,021
I told you, my wrist hurts!

290
00:20:21,591 --> 00:20:22,591
Knock, knock.

291
00:20:24,178 --> 00:20:25,190
Why are you coming in?

292
00:20:26,232 --> 00:20:27,505
We need to bring your fever down.

293
00:20:27,585 --> 00:20:28,858
I said don't!

294
00:20:34,872 --> 00:20:36,785
I can promise you this.

295
00:20:36,787 --> 00:20:39,501
Mai's doing just fine somewhere out there.

296
00:20:39,922 --> 00:20:41,098
And so is O Reum.

297
00:20:41,100 --> 00:20:42,459
What would you know?

298
00:20:42,591 --> 00:20:45,278
He took my daughter's bone marrow.
How could I not know?

299
00:20:45,325 --> 00:20:46,498
That damn...

300
00:20:47,825 --> 00:20:50,264
Stop taking your anger out on your mom.

301
00:20:50,445 --> 00:20:52,758
She deserves to be happy too.

302
00:20:53,352 --> 00:20:55,719
She would've been happy
if it weren't for you.

303
00:20:56,131 --> 00:20:57,858
And you have the nerve
to talk about happiness?

304
00:20:58,392 --> 00:21:00,306
Look at you.
You actually have a mouth on you.

305
00:21:02,614 --> 00:21:03,652
Yeah, you're right.

306
00:21:03,898 --> 00:21:06,204
I ruined her happiness.

307
00:21:06,651 --> 00:21:08,639
That's why I'm supporting her now.

308
00:21:08,641 --> 00:21:09,651
Easy for you to say...

309
00:21:12,792 --> 00:21:13,792
I'm sorry.

310
00:21:16,178 --> 00:21:17,357
I said I'm sorry.

311
00:21:18,575 --> 00:21:20,313
I remember...

312
00:21:20,847 --> 00:21:22,512
- how kind you used to be.
- Enough.

313
00:21:26,191 --> 00:21:27,203
I...

314
00:21:29,564 --> 00:21:31,827
This might sound a little crazy,

315
00:21:32,549 --> 00:21:34,873
but while we were raising Ji Ni,

316
00:21:34,957 --> 00:21:38,318
you know how sometimes
you start imagining things?

317
00:21:38,832 --> 00:21:40,945
What if one day, my husband and I...

318
00:21:40,947 --> 00:21:44,098
suddenly died in an accident?
What would happen to her?

319
00:21:44,591 --> 00:21:46,088
That's when I thought of you.

320
00:21:46,878 --> 00:21:49,473
I thought you would protect her.

321
00:21:50,350 --> 00:21:51,479
Funny, right?

322
00:21:52,355 --> 00:21:54,705
Yeah, real funny.
Does that even make sense?

323
00:21:55,265 --> 00:21:56,829
Why would I protect your daughter?

324
00:21:57,370 --> 00:22:00,411
Being the dependable eldest son,
with a lonely mom and a sick brother.

325
00:22:01,272 --> 00:22:04,394
That's more than enough to break anyone.
And now your daughter too?

326
00:22:05,842 --> 00:22:07,224
You've got some nerve.

327
00:22:08,485 --> 00:22:10,244
What am I, some tree
standing on the street?

328
00:22:11,052 --> 00:22:12,071
I was only...

329
00:22:12,972 --> 00:22:14,385
five years old back then.

330
00:22:17,558 --> 00:22:18,752
"Five years old."

331
00:22:20,079 --> 00:22:21,079
Yeah.

332
00:22:22,998 --> 00:22:24,671
You were a son
who had to be like a husband.

333
00:22:25,542 --> 00:22:28,491
- It must have been so hard.
- Just get out!

334
00:22:31,452 --> 00:22:33,127
We put such a heavy burden...

335
00:22:33,690 --> 00:22:35,796
on you when you were just a child.

336
00:22:36,252 --> 00:22:37,622
And it was my fault.

337
00:22:37,998 --> 00:22:40,890
That's why I wanted to apologize.

338
00:22:43,286 --> 00:22:44,466
I don't accept your apology.

339
00:22:44,772 --> 00:22:46,133
It's all in the past.

340
00:22:47,385 --> 00:22:48,790
So I don't need it anymore.

341
00:22:51,805 --> 00:22:52,858
Okay.

342
00:22:53,319 --> 00:22:54,325
I'll get going.

343
00:22:57,912 --> 00:22:58,990
But...

344
00:22:59,200 --> 00:23:00,535
at least eat some porridge.

345
00:23:01,272 --> 00:23:04,353
I think your mom made it for Mai.

346
00:23:04,765 --> 00:23:08,553
They say pork trotter porridge is
a postpartum recovery food in Vietnam.

347
00:23:08,978 --> 00:23:10,995
I think she made it for Mai,

348
00:23:11,413 --> 00:23:13,803
but Mai didn't get to eat any of it.

349
00:23:32,685 --> 00:23:33,856
Mai,

350
00:23:34,572 --> 00:23:35,663
where are you?

351
00:23:38,471 --> 00:23:39,618
O Reum,

352
00:23:41,308 --> 00:23:42,853
take me with you too.

353
00:23:53,265 --> 00:23:54,568
I never thought...

354
00:23:54,999 --> 00:23:57,045
I'd have a day like this.

355
00:23:58,451 --> 00:24:00,126
Do you really like me that much?

356
00:24:01,602 --> 00:24:02,643
Of course.

357
00:24:03,714 --> 00:24:04,714
Yeong Ju,

358
00:24:05,811 --> 00:24:07,583
I have a little dream.

359
00:24:08,092 --> 00:24:09,092
"A dream?"

360
00:24:09,392 --> 00:24:13,205
I inherited some money,
and I make pretty good money too,

361
00:24:13,207 --> 00:24:14,705
but I never have anyone to spend it on.

362
00:24:14,832 --> 00:24:17,705
Even when I went shopping
with my sister-in-law,

363
00:24:18,144 --> 00:24:20,039
it wasn't much fun.

364
00:24:20,118 --> 00:24:21,951
I had no woman to buy things for.

365
00:24:22,898 --> 00:24:23,951
But now...

366
00:24:24,259 --> 00:24:26,725
I'm so happy I have you, Yeong Ju.

367
00:24:28,152 --> 00:24:30,546
I'll buy you all kinds of pretty things,

368
00:24:31,275 --> 00:24:32,382
you can wear them here,

369
00:24:32,984 --> 00:24:34,187
and here too.

370
00:24:35,245 --> 00:24:36,245
I'll be like,

371
00:24:36,685 --> 00:24:39,508
"Isn't my woman gorgeous?
Aren't you jealous?"

372
00:24:40,662 --> 00:24:41,739
Sa Bin.

373
00:24:42,725 --> 00:24:44,379
But her whole life...

374
00:24:44,510 --> 00:24:47,210
is more beautiful than any jewel.

375
00:24:47,352 --> 00:24:49,298
I just want to show you off like this.

376
00:24:51,745 --> 00:24:54,519
I'm so glad I didn't die last year.

377
00:24:54,703 --> 00:24:56,190
Don't say things like that.

378
00:24:57,351 --> 00:24:59,697
There were so many times
I really wanted to die.

379
00:25:07,505 --> 00:25:09,006
Thank you for holding on.

380
00:25:10,832 --> 00:25:12,069
You did well.

381
00:25:12,492 --> 00:25:13,765
Come to me now.

382
00:25:29,018 --> 00:25:31,456
That's really all for today.

383
00:25:32,385 --> 00:25:34,234
Good night.

384
00:25:56,745 --> 00:25:58,001
Hey, get a grip.

385
00:26:00,532 --> 00:26:01,532
Il Dong.

386
00:26:05,892 --> 00:26:06,942
Are you crazy?

387
00:26:07,129 --> 00:26:09,403
Abandoned by your husband all your life,
and now you're losing your mind?

388
00:26:09,405 --> 00:26:10,405
Il Dong.

389
00:26:10,651 --> 00:26:12,085
I'm honestly speechless.

390
00:26:13,272 --> 00:26:14,712
You've got skills.

391
00:26:14,851 --> 00:26:16,548
How'd you land a younger bachelor?

392
00:26:16,625 --> 00:26:18,355
- I never would've guessed.
- You...

393
00:26:18,949 --> 00:26:19,978
know that guy?

394
00:26:20,878 --> 00:26:23,464
- How do you know Sa Bin?
- "Sa Bin..."

395
00:26:31,998 --> 00:26:34,035
How do you know him?

396
00:26:38,232 --> 00:26:40,617
He's the younger brother
of the general I work for.

397
00:26:40,965 --> 00:26:43,406
That place where
you pulled that proposal stunt today...

398
00:26:43,408 --> 00:26:45,161
belongs to the general.

399
00:26:45,456 --> 00:26:46,456
This can't be.

400
00:26:46,807 --> 00:26:47,807
That's right.

401
00:26:47,832 --> 00:26:50,198
Judging by that look on your face,
I don't need to explain any more.

402
00:26:50,625 --> 00:26:52,247
Turn him down, no questions asked,

403
00:26:52,276 --> 00:26:54,132
and help me knock some sense into him.

404
00:26:55,721 --> 00:26:57,898
Why aren't you saying anything?

405
00:26:59,071 --> 00:27:02,292
If you start talking nonsense again
about love and all that,

406
00:27:02,660 --> 00:27:04,475
I swear I'll make you regret it.

407
00:27:05,368 --> 00:27:06,557
Uncle.

408
00:27:07,204 --> 00:27:08,204
That's enough.

409
00:27:08,952 --> 00:27:11,489
Why do you get to decide
how my mom lives her life?

410
00:27:12,318 --> 00:27:14,091
Good, you're here.

411
00:27:14,145 --> 00:27:16,823
Hey, do you know who your mom's seeing?

412
00:27:16,825 --> 00:27:17,825
Korean medicine doctor.

413
00:27:18,365 --> 00:27:19,697
She picked a great one.

414
00:27:20,345 --> 00:27:21,354
Yeong Ju,

415
00:27:21,822 --> 00:27:22,822
you're the best.

416
00:27:23,022 --> 00:27:24,308
Give me a break.

417
00:27:24,412 --> 00:27:25,896
Get a grip, you idiot!

418
00:27:25,898 --> 00:27:27,525
He's the general's brother.

419
00:27:29,318 --> 00:27:31,224
The general...

420
00:27:31,499 --> 00:27:32,785
- you work for?
- Yeah.

421
00:27:32,898 --> 00:27:34,731
Getting the picture now?

422
00:27:41,792 --> 00:27:43,052
Yeong Ju, you're home?

423
00:27:57,985 --> 00:27:59,573
Who is this woman?

424
00:28:04,078 --> 00:28:06,811
That damn woman?

425
00:28:25,269 --> 00:28:28,422
(Family Register)

426
00:28:28,458 --> 00:28:30,341
What on earth is this mess?

427
00:28:30,343 --> 00:28:31,811
Perfect timing.

428
00:28:32,178 --> 00:28:34,412
Keep your mom in check.
She's not getting remarried. Got it?

429
00:28:34,414 --> 00:28:37,616
He's off with that Ji Ni or whatever,
rubbing his magic lamp.

430
00:28:37,618 --> 00:28:39,330
You've got to nip this in the bud.

431
00:28:39,332 --> 00:28:40,945
You really don't want
Mom to get remarried?

432
00:28:40,947 --> 00:28:42,138
If it's a bad idea, don't do it.

433
00:28:42,140 --> 00:28:43,992
What kind of dream was I having?

434
00:28:43,993 --> 00:28:46,068
Happiness was never meant for me.

435
00:28:46,070 --> 00:28:48,565
Really?
You're Lieutenant No's older sister?

436
00:28:49,868 --> 00:28:51,868
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
